.TH TERMNAV 1 "August 2026" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termnav \- route terminal navigation, focus, links, and editor opens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termnav
is one native command for navigation across Neovim, tmux, SSH, WezTerm, and
VS Code terminal boundaries. Integrations should invoke the structured
subcommands below instead of reproducing routing policy.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B navigate
Route pane selection, tab selection, or tab movement through the nearest
available scope.
.TP
.B relay
Send or serve the connection-scoped Unix relay protocol. The send form uses
the same pane-select, tab-select, and tab-move actions as navigate. Serve and
commit forms are internal integration interfaces.
.TP
.B ssh
Run one requested SSH session with its reverse-forward relay. Termnav never
opens a second authenticated transport connection.
.TP
.B link-host
Print the host represented by the current terminal context for semantic links.
.TP
.B tmux context
Publish tmux ownership metadata to one exact terminal client.
.TP
.B tmux focus
Publish and maintain hierarchical focus leases between adjacent tmux layers.
.TP
.B tmux follow-click
Resolve tmux mouse metadata to a browser URL or Neovim file target.
.TP
.B nvim open
Open a local or remote target in the narrowest eligible Neovim scope.
.TP
.B nvim ssh-open
Reuse one exact existing SSH ControlMaster without network fallback.
.TP
.B vscode focus
Publish an authenticated, ordered Neovim focus lease to a VS Code window.
.TP
.B eza
Run eza with remote-aware OSC-8 file hyperlinks.
.TP
.B version
Print the timestamp and commit identity embedded at build time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/termnav-UID
Owner-only relay, navigation, and focus coordination state.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nvim-tmux-open
Neovim socket registry shared with the editor integration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR nvim (1)
